$\begin{align}
&\phantom{=}\displaystyle\lim_{x\to\infty}\dfrac{6x}{15x-8}
\\\\
&=\displaystyle\lim_{x\to\infty}\dfrac{\dfrac{d}{dx}\left[6x\right]}{\dfrac{d}{dx}[15x-8]}\qquad\gray{\text{l’Hôpital’s rule}}
\\\\
&=\displaystyle\lim_{x\to\infty}\dfrac{6}{15}
\\\\
&=0.4
\end{align}$

Note that we were only able to use l’Hôpital’s rule because the limit $\displaystyle\lim_{x\to\infty}\dfrac{\dfrac{d}{dx}\left[6x\right]}{\dfrac{d}{dx}[15x-8]}$ can actually be determined.
